PROJECT={'id':'ex-5-project-source141','qNo':'Project','question':'Create an artwork or real-world model demonstrating a topic from this unit, by hand or with technology.','steps':['Choose motion of a car around a circular track as a model; this is one sample project, not the textbook’s only acceptable outcome.','Set a position vector r⃗(t) = 10cos tî+10sin tĵ metres, using t in seconds and angles in radians.','Draw the circular track of radius 10 m and mark the car at t = 0, π/2, π, 3π/2.','Differentiate: v⃗(t) = −10sin tî+10cos tĵ m/s. Draw each velocity arrow tangent to the track.','Its speed is |v⃗| = 10 m/s. Draw unit directions −sin tî+cos tĵ.','Differentiate again: a⃗(t) = −10cos tî−10sin tĵ m/s², pointing toward the centre.','Label position, velocity, speed and acceleration clearly; add the source roadway photograph as inspiration. Explain how a car can change velocity while maintaining constant speed.'],'answer':'A labelled circular-motion model with checked position, tangent velocity, speed 10 m/s and inward acceleration magnitude 10 m/s².','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement — sample project','sourceReferences':[{'page':141,'jpg':'075_page_1.jpg','verification':'full source open-ended instruction and dedicated photograph checked'}]}
